00:07:05.951 --> 00:07:06.818
- [Voiceover] Tim asks,

00:07:06.818 --> 00:07:08.559
"You've joked about being overstaffed,

00:07:08.559 --> 00:07:09.674
"but what's the balance between hiring

00:07:09.674 --> 00:07:11.432
"for capacity and waste?"

00:07:13.156 --> 00:07:13.980
- Tim, that's a great question.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.280
For all of you that are growing quickly,

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.556
I think one of the things
I take the most pride in

00:07:17.556 --> 00:07:20.992
is my ability to have a
pulse on my organization

00:07:20.992 --> 00:07:23.639
from a sales top-line revenue impact,

00:07:23.639 --> 00:07:26.079
and on the bottom-line cost thing.

00:07:26.079 --> 00:07:28.155
I think I grow businesses way faster.

00:07:28.155 --> 00:07:30.720
I do believe that if I end up
operating two more businesses,

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.112
if I have four businesses
in my career before I die,

00:07:33.112 --> 00:07:36.630
that I've hypergrown, I
have two now in my bag,

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:40.379
like, really fast, like,
all-time, like, really,

00:07:40.379 --> 00:07:42.318
especially non-technology
companies, really fast,

00:07:42.318 --> 00:07:44.675
I will be known, I mean,
I actually think my legacy

00:07:44.675 --> 00:07:47.936
as an operator could be speed to victory.

00:07:49.486 --> 00:07:52.047
I think what I'm really good
at is I have disproportional

00:07:52.047 --> 00:07:54.159
understanding of the
pulse of what I'm selling,

00:07:54.159 --> 00:07:56.946
and I'm willing to bet right to the brink,

00:07:56.946 --> 00:07:58.826
because I don't need to
take home a lot of money.

00:07:58.826 --> 00:08:00.359
Like, I've always left my own moneys

00:08:00.359 --> 00:08:03.644
and my own vices on the
table to reinvest back

00:08:03.644 --> 00:08:05.362
into my business, which
allows me to overstaff,

00:08:05.362 --> 00:08:08.145
which means I'm them
ready for the new business

00:08:08.145 --> 00:08:09.965
that comes in, and I
don't have to go crazy

00:08:09.965 --> 00:08:12.486
finding the talent, and so,

00:08:12.486 --> 00:08:13.726
because I'm trying to build culture, sure,

00:08:13.726 --> 00:08:15.526
you can freelance and
outsource less margin,

00:08:15.526 --> 00:08:17.406
but you can do better cash
role, make more profit,

00:08:17.406 --> 00:08:19.148
but I want those people part of my team,

00:08:19.148 --> 00:08:22.526
and grow with them, let them
learn the religion, grow.

00:08:22.526 --> 00:08:26.008
So, I think everybody's
got their own balance,

00:08:26.008 --> 00:08:28.562
but I think it's completely
predicated on your stomach

00:08:28.562 --> 00:08:31.267
for risk, because it comes with risk,

00:08:31.267 --> 00:08:33.322
you don't wanna overstaff,
then you lose an account

00:08:33.322 --> 00:08:35.272
and you have to let people
go, that changes the vibe.

00:08:36.592 --> 00:08:38.825
I think it comes down to
your salesmanship ability,

00:08:38.825 --> 00:08:41.192
can you always, in a
pinch, sell some more stuff

00:08:41.192 --> 00:08:43.990
out of nowhere, and I
think that it comes down to

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.553
the understanding of where
your business is positioned

00:08:48.553 --> 00:08:50.991
compared to the landscape, meaning,

00:08:50.991 --> 00:08:53.232
I always knew that I'm
ahead of the market,

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:54.764
and the world's gonna come to me.

00:08:54.764 --> 00:08:58.351
A lot of our scopes,
our contracts for 2016,

00:08:58.351 --> 00:09:01.253
are growing very quickly,
because I knew the world in 2009

00:09:01.253 --> 00:09:03.447
would spend more money on
Facebook, Twitter, Tumblr,

00:09:03.447 --> 00:09:05.467
Pinterest, Instagram,
Snapchat, or whatever was there

00:09:05.467 --> 00:09:07.511
at the time, you know, the current state

00:09:07.511 --> 00:09:09.368
of the internet, so I'm riding that wave.

00:09:09.368 --> 00:09:11.052
It lets me bet a little bit more.

00:09:12.152 --> 00:09:15.334
It's a pulse-cadence feel, taste thing

00:09:15.334 --> 00:09:16.634
that allows me to get away with it,

00:09:16.634 --> 00:09:18.051
but ultimately, more than anything,

00:09:18.051 --> 00:09:21.173
it's the balance of your own selfish wants

00:09:21.173 --> 00:09:23.867
of your take-home income,
versus how much you wanna

00:09:23.867 --> 00:09:25.225
reinvest in your business.

00:09:25.225 --> 00:09:26.026
It's as simple as that.

00:09:26.026 --> 00:09:27.384
If you're running a
business and you're making

00:09:27.384 --> 00:09:29.113
a million dollars in revenue, and you have

00:09:29.113 --> 00:09:32.550
$600,000 in expenses,
you're taking home $400,000.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.778
You could make it $850,000 in expenses,

00:09:35.778 --> 00:09:38.482
take home $150,000,
and then know that that

00:09:38.482 --> 00:09:40.038
extra investment will allow
you to make three million

00:09:40.038 --> 00:09:41.280
the next year.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.080
I believe in myself ultimately,

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.378
any entrepreneur, CEO, or decision maker

00:09:45.378 --> 00:09:47.096
that's taking money off the table,

00:09:47.096 --> 00:09:49.882
I believe is betting less
on themselves along the way

00:09:49.882 --> 00:09:51.601
and are playing a short-term game.

00:09:52.691 --> 00:09:54.097
To me, the time I start extracting dollars

00:09:54.097 --> 00:09:57.191
is when I believe less in
the growth of the company.

